    "summary": "- A renewal moves the period and stores its invoice in one atomic store step. Only the call that wins that step charges, so concurrent or repeated `RenewDue` calls create at most one invoice and take at most one charge per (subscription, period start).\n- A gateway outage during renewal still advances the period, leaves the invoice open, and keeps the subscription's status, with no error returned. Other subscriptions still renew when one fails, and `RenewDue` returns the joined errors after trying all of them.\n- New tests cover concurrent renewal, a gateway outage followed by a second run, and \n...[truncated]",
